alex_m: Customer on Cloudflare Workers edge runtime — streaming ReadableStream stalls after ~12-20s and we see intermittent 401 mid-stream, sometimes a 410 Gone. They gave a short repro and a recording.

alex_m: Repro gist (TS edge):
```ts
const res = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood-alpha' });
const reader = (res.body as ReadableStream).getReader();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  console.log(new TextDecoder().decode(value));
}
```
Customer says output sometimes contains truncated UTF-8 chunks and then connection errors + a 401 JSON response mid-stream.

priya_s: Which SDK version are they on? Any proxy in front? Also did they use token rotation or short-lived credentials?

alex_m: They bundled with esbuild; package.json shows "@redwood/inference": "0.1.4" in their app. They use short-lived tokens (ttl ~30s) and a sidecar that rotates tokens.

sam_dev: Two quick thoughts: (1) Edge runtimes can't re-open an existing ReadableStream when a token rotates — retries that try to re-auth mid-stream will break. (2) Old SDK edge build had slightly different streaming boundary handling (utf8 chunking). Both could explain truncated frames + auth failures.

ryan_oncall: Can you reproduce locally with a Worker-like environment? Try curl -N to mirror what the edge sees:

curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" "https://api.redwood.example/v1/stream?model=redwood-alpha"

Look for an immediate 200 + SSE frames then a sudden 401/410 JSON payload.

priya_s: Ask customer to check their bundler output to confirm the edge bundle target and to upgrade SDK to latest edge build. Also suggest disabling automatic streaming retries while we debug.

sam_dev: Suggestion to mitigate: ensure token lifetime > expected stream length or implement header-based in-band token refresh (mint a single stream token with long expiry). Also set client option to turn off in-stream retries.

```ts
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  edge: true,
  disableStreamingRetries: true
});
```

sam_dev: Short-term patch we recommend to customer: upgrade to 0.2.1-edge (edge build fixes chunk boundary encoding), disable streaming retries, and increase token TTL. If they cannot increase TTL, use a streaming proxy that performs an authenticated one-time request and proxies the bytes to the edge runtime.

alex_m: Customer upgraded to 0.2.1-edge and disabled retries — reported big improvement but still seeing rare 410 after ~30s for very long responses.

ryan_oncall: 410 usually indicates an intermediate (Cloudflare) closing the connection. Ask customer to try small keepalive pings or reduce upstream idle timeout. Also capture tcpdump / worker logs for the closing event.

priya_s: I'll open an infra ticket to check our edge termination rules and long-lived connection SLOs. Also requesting logs for the two sample request IDs the customer provided.

support-bot: Ticket created: INC-2345. Assigned to eng-runtime and oncall.

alex_m: Thanks — I'll send the sample request IDs and the customer's bundler output. Will follow up once infra confirms. :thumbsup:
